From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:32:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-298: revert lane 302 lever 12 (small-n split_k) from
 v0.1.3.2: it changes plain greedy text vs v0.1.3.1

Reverts c8446c32d0, c1079d3153 (code + test arm) and the protected-win entry 1d346fdfd4 + its re-key 8c71293db7
(vulkan-mm-splitk-small-n-verify removed from protected-wins.json). Resolution rows e062ff7580 stay as history.
Conflict in protected-wins.json (lever 13 entry 5c747ded24 sits after it): kept the body 6 entry, dropped the
split_k entry only. Code check: diff d78f1890b7..this in ggml/src/ggml-vulkan + tests has the same patch-id as
lever 13 alone (5de60bda7e..b5899b523c), 8e28c7f7b4.

Why: rg132 fn + orn BLOCKER (plain greedy chat text moved vs v0.1.3.1, deterministic per side). Untimed bisect
rg-bis-10101451 on the b5899b523c build: GGML_ARIFI_MM_SPLITK_SMALLN=0 restores v0.1.3.1 text on both models (fn
chat/code/json/reason, orn chat/code); IQ2S_BODY=5 alone does not. Pre-ruled HQ86 13:02 + HQ87 14:5x (Q87
correction accepted): lever 12 fails its rule = revert. HQ87 15:2x: lane 302 builds an order-preserving exact
split_k; it lands later as a fresh pick through its own bars.

Origin: lane-298 (revert of lane-302 lever 12, HQ87 2026-10-10 14:5x ruling)
Measured-effect: correctness only - restores v0.1.3.1 plain greedy ids on Flash-Next + Ornith 1.5 (cache/mtp-x1-lane/cells/rg-bis-10101451-state.json, BIS-READ in cache/mtp-x1-lane/progress.txt)
